Add board support for Xiaomi Redmi Note 13 4G (sapphire / SM6225 / bengal).
Includes:
- bsd/dev/sweet_board.h: sweet_board_sapphire() runtime board detection matching "xiaomi,sapphire"
- iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp: SM6225 DPU MMIO base 0x05e00000 (verified from ios-sapphire live FDT)
- iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp: disable SweetAdreno630 user client on sapphire (Adreno 610
  uses CPU software rendering / Mesa path)
- bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c: allow SPMI reads on SID 2 for PM7250B battery/charger peripherals on sapphire
- iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetBattery.cpp: pollSapphire() reading PM7250B QG fuel gauge (0x4800) and SMB5 charger (0x1000)
- bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c: sapphire PM6125 (SID 0) GPIO5 volume-up button (0x0c4, base 0xc400)
- bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c: bit-banged FocalTech FT3519T driver on sapphire
  (QUP0 SE2 0x04a88000, TLMM WEST 0x00500000, SDA GPIO 6, SCL GPIO 7, IRQ GPIO 80, reset GPIO 86, AVDD enable GPIO 36)

